<article class="env-lemma" id="08XQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08XQ">Lemma <span data-tag="08XQ">47.3.2</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a flat ring map. If $E$ is an injective $S$-module, then $E$ is injective as an $R$-module. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ R(M, E) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ S(M \otimes _ R S, E)$ by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/05DQ" data-tag="05DQ">10.14.3</a> and the fact that tensoring with $S$ is exact. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>